A||||2||Wannabe||3800 swap - Camaro 5spd ECM||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||03-12-2001||03:40 PM||||From all I've been able to find by searching through old posts, there doesn't seem to be a  clear solution to the problem of using a '95+ Series II 3800 with a manual trans. Has anybody looked into using the computer from a 3800 Camaro in place of the one that comes with the front drive/auto combination? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||03-12-2001||04:32 PM||||Check with ACE in CO. They did my Series II 3800 with 5 sp and I have had no problems , 40K miles so far||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||03-12-2001||07:19 PM||||See if the computer is the 16193247 and if the 3800 was available with a manual trans. Might not have been. <P>There is absolutely no reference to a manual transmission option in the 94/95 16193247 ECM used with the 3800 engines in the FWD appliations.<P>The 3800 Camaro might be a flash PCM too. In the 93-95 time frame, they got rather goofy as to which one they used. <P>I have two Series II SC engines running on the 94/95 Series I ECM but there is no stall saver so stalling on a throttle snap closed could still occur.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
